It does seem strange that such a crappy weapon as Stormbringer costs 
$8000 whereas Demonbane a first-class longsword (as good as Frostbrand 
according to the artifact spoiler) rates only  $2500, and Excalibur also 
not very good (but useful) rates $4500.

My Valkyrie acquaintance has decided after some  experimentation, that 
the best combination  of weapons  for use, avoiding too much weight is ;

1.	Mjollnir as main
2.	Demonbane as backup
3.	Frostbrand as reserve backup
4.	about 9 or 12 +6 or higher elven daggers for throwing.

Reasons:

Mj is powerful and has the advantage of being a ranged weapon so that 
one can keep away from many foes whilst dealing with them. Elven daggers 
  seem to do quite a bit of damage and thrown with gauntlets of power 
finish of lots of nasties before they can get anywhere near. They don't 
seem to suffer damage, although they are shown as wood so it does not 
seem necessary to foo-proof them. In fact this has not been tried in my 
limited experience-any enlightenment would be interesting. Silver 
daggers would be interesting, but having never seen any Tina has to make 
do with elven.
For major foes, Demonbane seems better than Frost brand because its x2 
is guaranteed for demons, but Frostbrand sometimes fails in that 
respect. FB is good at first, but Tina likes to use Demonbane later on 
as backup. We assume +7 for the weapons and expert for hammer, longsword 
and dagger, luckstone carried and gauntlets of power at +5

These suggestions are not quite in line with the weapon spoiler-what do 
other newbies think ?

The main thing is to use ranged weapons first-daggers then MJ, and if 
they fail (spells being ignored) Demonbane or FB are wielded.



